From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:00:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: apple,pmgr-pwrstate: add
 apple,bridge-link

A consumer-switched power state can have a bus bridge in front of the
block it powers. The bridge's two link words must have bit 0 cleared
before the state powers off and set again once it is on, and they are
only accessible while the state is on. Describe where they are: a
phandle to the block's node, the index of its register range and the
offset of the words in that range. The PMGR driver can then do that as
part of the consumer's power-off and power-on.

The T8132 external display system domains need it.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 803e497819df4b13c5f8dbc221ebdfd07e40befd)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml   | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml
index 420f47e452..6612c626e8 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmgr-pwrstate.yaml
@@ -42,6 +42,12 @@ allOf:
     then:
       required:
         - apple,consumer-switched
+  - if:
+      required:
+        - apple,bridge-link
+    then:
+      required:
+        - apple,consumer-switched
 
 description: |
   Apple SoCs include PMGR blocks responsible for power management,
@@ -179,6 +185,21 @@ properties:
         - description: value while the domain is off
     maxItems: 4
 
+  apple,bridge-link:
+    description:
+      The two consecutive 32-bit link words of the bus bridge of the block
+      behind this consumer-switched domain, as the node of that block, the
+      index of one of its reg entries and the offset of the words from the
+      start of that entry. Bit 0 of each is cleared before the domain powers
+      off and set after it has powered on. The words are only accessible
+      while the domain is on.
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
+    items:
+      - items:
+          - description: node of the block behind the domain
+          - description: index of a reg entry of that node
+          - description: offset of the link words from the start of that entry
+
   apple,inherited-on:
     description: |
       On T8132, the boot loader hands over an active domain whose state
